spec: BACKLOG "Flakes observed" (recorded by di-deploy's gate, 2026-09-09)

why: three tests in TestResilienceTimed assert "no second attempt" with
  Thread.sleep(60) after a 20 ms hedge delay. Under load the first
  attempt takes longer than the delay, the timer fires as designed and
  starts=2. The file's own header says every assertion is about ORDER,
  never elapsed time; these three break that rule.

what: a ManualTimer in the test (after records the callback, cancel
  forgets it, fireAll runs what survived), passed explicitly to
  Hedge.run; the assertion becomes the real contract — after the first
  attempt settled, firing every armed timer starts nothing, because
  `done` guards start(). Three sleeps gone. Not touching Hedge itself.

next: write ManualTimer, rewrite the three tests, verify old-vs-new
